    "q-1344": {
      "dom_id": "step-q1344",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $u⊥v$, find the value of $a.$",
      "worked_solution": "We know that $u⊥v$ ($a$ and $b$ are perpendicular) if and only if $u\\cdot v=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{x}\\cdot {v}_{x}+{u}_{y}\\cdot {v}_{y} \\\\  & =a\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =a-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ a-8 & =0 \\\\ a & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
